{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The GATT identifiers and characteristic values the iPad publishes and the Mac helper reads."}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The iPad app and the Mac helper ship separately, so the identifiers and value formats they share live here in one Foundation-only module, and the helper links none of the HID code. HeadwireGATTContract owns the service and characteristic UUIDs, the source mode request the iPad publishes to ask the Mac for a video mode, and the pairing offer and answer that let the helper link pair over an encrypted Bluetooth link with no code. Each value starts with a version byte, and readers ignore bytes they do not know. It does not publish anything or talk to CoreBluetooth; HeadwireHID publishes the services, and the helper reads them."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Identifiers","anchor":"Identifiers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/GATTContract"]},{"title":"Source mode","anchor":"Source-mode","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/SourceModeRequest","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/SourceModeWireError"]},{"title":"Pairing","anchor":"Pairing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOffer","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingAnswer","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOfferWireError"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiregattcontract"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadat